=== {{etymology}} ===
Invented by the translation team at KIST and e-tools.
Meaning '''one who does not make mistakes'''.
Used to describe the [[digital]] mudasobwa. According to the 1st Kinyarwanda-English Dictionary called "IRIZA-STARTER 2006" compiled by Rural ICT-Net, The coined
word "mudasobwa" for a computer appears in the poem "Imanzi yanyuze u Rwanda" on the 25th anniversary of Mgr
Aloys Bigirumwami's priesthood (It was o n the 25 July 1976) where it says: "Ubwo ari Nkoni iragiye Nyundo Uracyure
impenda iyo zagenewe, Ubwo uri Mudasobwa ntusobanure intama, Uraturagire inkome dukomere ku Mana, Komeza kudushora amariba adakama Nkumburwa ya Nkomejekurinda."

